From: Codex <codex@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] uxtheme: send a per-window theme change number from SetWindowTheme

Purpose: let XP's native controls reopen their theme after SetWindowTheme.
XP's comctl32 v6 controls remember the change number in WM_THEMECHANGED's
wParam and reopen their theme only when it differs. Wine sent 0, the
number the controls start with, so the folder window's ReBar closed its
theme after Explorer's SetWindowTheme(rebar, "ExplorerToolbar") and never
reopened it: its band labels were drawn black on the classic face colour
instead of the theme's grey text over the toolbar background. Sending -1,
as a per-window change, makes the ReBar reopen its theme; its labels and
background then match the reference XP machine. Only the opted-in
external shell is affected.

diff --git a/dlls/uxtheme/system.c b/dlls/uxtheme/system.c
index 2f90dbb..10ec8c0 100644
--- a/dlls/uxtheme/system.c
+++ b/dlls/uxtheme/system.c
@@ -733,7 +733,12 @@ HRESULT WINAPI SetWindowTheme(HWND hwnd, LPCWSTR pszSubAppName,
     if (SUCCEEDED(hr)) UXTHEME_InstallExternalClock(hwnd, pszSubAppName, pszSubIdList);
     if (SUCCEEDED(hr)) UXTHEME_InstallExternalRebar(hwnd, pszSubAppName, pszSubIdList);
     if(SUCCEEDED(hr))
-        SendMessageW(hwnd, WM_THEMECHANGED, 0, 0);
+    {
+        /* XP's comctl32 v6 controls keep the change number from wParam and
+         * reopen their theme only when it differs; a per-window change sends -1. */
+        WPARAM change = GetEnvironmentVariableW(L"WIN4WINE_EXTERNAL_SHELL", NULL, 0) ? (WPARAM)-1 : 0;
+        SendMessageW(hwnd, WM_THEMECHANGED, change, 0);
+    }
     return hr;
 }
 
